  "title": { "en": "Health and body", "uz": "Salomatlik va tana", "ru": "Здоровье и тело", "tr": "Sağlık ve vücut" },
  "goal": {
    "en": "Name parts of the body, say what hurts and give advice with \"should\".",
    "uz": "Tana a'zolarini ayting, qayeringiz og'riyotganini tushuntiring va \"should\" bilan maslahat bering.",
    "ru": "Назовите части тела, скажите, что у вас болит, и дайте совет с \"should\".",
    "tr": "Vücudun bölümlerini söyle, nerenin ağrıdığını anlat ve \"should\" ile tavsiye ver."
  },
  "guide": "nubi",
  "color": "#DC2626",
  "tip": {
    "title": { "en": "I have a headache, you should rest", "uz": "I have a headache, you should rest", "ru": "I have a headache, you should rest", "tr": "I have a headache, you should rest" },
    "body": {
      "en": "To talk about an illness, English uses \"have a\": I have a headache. I have a fever. For a part of the body use \"hurts\": My leg hurts. To give advice, use \"should\" + verb with no \"to\": You should rest. \"Should\" never changes: He should rest. Negative: should not (shouldn't). Question: Should I rest?",
      "uz": "Kasallik haqida gapirganda ingliz tilida \"have a\" ishlatiladi: I have a headache (so'zma-so'z: menda bosh og'rig'i bor). Tana a'zosi bilan \"hurts\" keladi: My leg hurts. O'zbekchadagi \"... kerak\" maslahati ingliz tilida \"should\" + fe'l bilan beriladi, \"to\" qo'yilmaydi: You should rest. \"Should\" hech qachon o'zgarmaydi: He should rest. Inkor: should not (shouldn't). Savol: Should I rest?",
      "ru": "О болезни по-английски говорят с \"have a\": I have a headache (дословно: я имею головную боль), а не \"у меня болит\". С частью тела используется \"hurts\": My leg hurts. Совет дают с \"should\" + глагол без \"to\": You should rest. \"Should\" никогда не меняется: He should rest. Отрицание: should not (shouldn't). Вопрос: Should I rest?",
      "tr": "İngilizcede hastalıktan söz ederken \"have a\" kullanılır: I have a headache (kelimesi kelimesine: bir baş ağrım var). Vücudun bir yeri için \"hurts\" denir: My leg hurts. Tavsiye verirken Türkçedeki -meli / -malı eki yerine \"should\" + fiil gelir, \"to\" kullanılmaz: You should rest. \"Should\" hiç değişmez: He should rest. Olumsuz: should not (shouldn't). Soru: Should I rest?"
    },
    "examples": [
      { "en": "I have a headache.", "native": { "uz": "Mening boshim og'riyapti.", "ru": "У меня болит голова.", "tr": "Başım ağrıyor." } },
      { "en": "My leg hurts.", "native": { "uz": "Mening oyog'im og'riyapti.", "ru": "У меня болит нога.", "tr": "Bacağım ağrıyor." } },
      { "en": "You should rest.", "native": { "uz": "Sen dam olishing kerak.", "ru": "Тебе следует отдохнуть.", "tr": "Dinlenmelisin." } }
    ]
  },
